0..73 Comment "/// This source states the circle\'s loop space and its equivalence with a"
74..107 Comment "/// presentation of the integers."
108..111 Comment "///"
112..182 Comment "/// The loop words and the integers describe the same paths at `Base`."
183..243 Comment "/// Winding and spinning prove the round trips by induction."
244..298 Comment "/// Both round trips need no interval and owe nothing."
299..302 Comment "///"
303..364 Comment "/// The lowering mints the cancellation rules for loop words."
365..425 Comment "/// The kernel checks each round trip against the path types"
426..450 Comment "/// in the presentation."
451..519 Comment "/// `Path.step`, `Path.back` and `Path.ap` take their path type from"
520..536 Comment "/// the words of"
537..614 Comment "/// their operands, so this source annotates none of them. A cell between two"
615..670 Comment "/// distinct points would need that type written again."
671..674 Comment "///"
675..724 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/loop-space.gandr"
725..731 Keyword "import"
